[A7][D][F#7]partakes [Gsus][G][D]one [Bm][A][D]holy [E7][A]food,
[A][D]and [A7]to [D][G]one [D]hope [Bm][B]she [Em]presses,
[A][D][G]with [D][Gmaj7][Em]every [G][Em7][D]grace [A7][D]endued.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D][G]Though [D][A7]with [D][Em]a [D][A7]scornful [D]wonder
[A7][D][F#7]we [Gsus][G]see [D][Bm]her [A][D]sore [E7][A]oppressed,
[A][D][A7]by [D][G]schisms [D][Bm]rent [B][Em]asunder,
[A][D][G][D]by [Gmaj7][Em][G][Em7]heresies [D][A7][D]distressed,
[D][G]yet [D]saints [A7][D]their [Em]watch [D][A7]are [D]keeping;
[A7][D]their [F#7][Gsus]cry [G][D]goes [Bm][A]up, [D][E7]"How [A]long?"
[A][D]And [A7]soon [D][G]the [D]night [Bm][B]of [Em]weeping
[A][D]shall [G][D]be [Gmaj7][Em]the [G][Em7]morn [D][A7]of [D]song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D][G][D]'Mid [A7][D]toil [Em][D]and [A7][D]tribulation,
[A7][D][F#7]and [Gsus][G]tumult [D][Bm]of [A][D]her [E7][A]war,
